==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Madoka & Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Ultimate Madoka''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Madoka can be used the same way as [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Aphrodite]] (to snipe enemies from the backline), just with a different target trait and ability. Her range is lower, but has more DPS and some crowd control to compensate.

Madoka is also faster than Aphrodite, but this speed can lead her into the attack range of the enemy, so be cautious when sending her out against melee pushers. On the other hand, her speed can be useful for getting into blind spots of certain enemies like [[Queen B]] (such as she can then snipe other nasty enemies behind Queen B like [[THE SLOTH]]), making her speed a double-edged sword.

==='''True Form'''===
In addition to improved stats, Madoka swaps Strong for Massive Damage while gaining two new targets in Zombie and Relic, along with Zombie Killer and Curse Immunity to aid her new matchups. Her usage remains mostly the same as her previous forms: although she sheds some of her survivability, Massive Damage dramatically increases her damage against her target traits and doubles down on her role as a backline nuker with a side of crowd control. Her new matchups against Zombies and Relics are favorable as she outranges the vast majority of them, but their burrowing and massive pushing power respectively mean one must be careful to not let them into Madoka's sizeable blind spot.

Note that although Madoka's damage per hit increases with her True Form, her attack cycle is also slightly longer, resulting in a minuscule DPS increase. Nevertheless, this is a minor drawback at worst, as her Massive Damage ability patches that by packing a much bigger punch with every hit.

{{Job|Classification = Crowd-Controller & Sniper|TrueClass = Nuker & Sniper|UltraClass=}}

